  "body": "Guard the LinuxCNC probe tolerance check with the task parameter `#<_task> EQ 1`.\nIn backplot preview, probe values are simulated or zero. The check stops the\npreview with M2 when `#<_task>` is not checked. With this guard, the preview\ncontinues and shows the toolpath. The tolerance check still stops the machine during\nlive execution when `#<_task>` is 1.\n\nIgnore whitespace within keywords when checking comment strings against active keywords.\nAdd PYRELOAD to the active keyword regular expression. LinuxCNC accepts keywords\nwith spaces and lower-case letters. The comment guard preserves keyword boundaries\nfor arguments like file names and prefixes active comments with a dash to keep them inert.\nPlain text like Message and Python stays unchanged.\n\nReason for new test binary:\n- `crates/post/tests/linuxcnc_post.rs`: Dedicated integration suite for LinuxCNC post processor output, safety blocks, and comment guards against the JS engine.\n\nReadings:\n- LinuxCNC G-code Reference (Messages, Comments, Named Parameters #<_task>)\n\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/post/tests/linuxcnc_post.rs`:\n  - `probe_measure_check_guarded_by_task_parameter`\n  - `active_comment_guard_catches_spaced_keywords_and_pyreload`\n\nWhat was not exercised:\n- Hardware execution on a physical CNC machine running LinuxCNC.\n\nChangelog: LinuxCNC post guards probe measure check in preview mode and catches active comment keywords with spaces and PYRELOAD.\n\nFixes #4152\n",
